  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Delta;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>ve therefore, increase in pressure will bring reaction in forward direction.<br /><br />In option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C&nbsp;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo></math> as the reaction is exothermic therefore, increase in temperature will decrease the equilibrium constant.<br /><br />In option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D&nbsp;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo></math> Equilibrium constant changes only with temperature.<br /><br />Hence, option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are correct. Therefore, option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is incorrect choice.",
